@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-validity`

-- g2-second-schedule.l4: the Second Schedule of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025 (the "Trainings" schedule, referred to by s 6(a)(4)), as data and as the
-- engine that reads it.
--
-- IMPORTS.  prelude, daydate, il-interpretation-time and domain, and g2-validity (a group-internal import, for "holds
-- a licence of grade N": a licence counts only if it is in force).  No module of another group is imported.
--
-- HOW THE SCHEDULE READS.  Three Parts, one per kind of licence sought (A grade 1, B grade 2, C grade 3).  Each Part is
-- a table of items; every item has COLUMN A (prior training or experience: any one of the entries listed), COLUMN B
-- (what is required for the licence sought: any one of the entries listed, for items 1 of Parts A and B; otherwise one
-- requirement) and COLUMN C (notes: the three-year note on the experience items).  Every figure of "up to N hours" is
-- the ceiling of a course the Training Division runs (trap T6), not a count the applicant must reach.
--
-- THE DATA.  Each of the 17 items is one named constant below, under the quotation of its own lines of inputs/law.wiki,
-- checked against the gazette (Sefer HaChukim 3349, pp. 201 to 205, viewed as page images).  Two differences between
-- the wiki and the gazette were found in this Schedule: (1) Part C item 4: the wiki puts the sentence "training of up to
-- 240 hours ..." in column A, opened by a stray bracket, and leaves column B empty; the gazette (p. 204) puts it in
-- column B as in every other row.  THE GAZETTE GOVERNS (fork FS6).  (2) Part A item 3, column B: the wiki line stops one word
-- short of the gazette's (p. 201), which adds the last word of the Division's full name ("vocational training"): a dropped word, no legal effect.
--
-- FORKS REGISTERED IN THIS MODULE (full text in FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2).  Each reading is a field of
-- `Reading of the Second Schedule`, and the alternative is the same engine called with another value:
--   FS1 (T1)   B3(2) and C3(2), C4(2) name a certificate by grade; B5(1), A3 and C6 name "a certificate in refrigeration
--              and air-conditioning studies from the Training Division", with no grade.  TAKEN: the ungraded entry covers
--              every Training Division certificate that no graded entry of the same Part names (graded over general), so
--              no Division certificate is covered by two items and each graded item keeps a purpose.  ALTERNATIVE: the ungraded entry
--              covers every Division certificate of any grade, so the graded holder is in two items with different hours.
--              Since the D1 repair (2026-10-14) this reading has one exception, fork FS10: the Division certificate that the
--              course of the Part sought itself confers is not a column A entry of the ungraded rows A3, B5(1) and C6.
--   FS10        The Division certificate of the grade sought (grade 1 for a grade 1 licence, 2 for 2, 3 for 3) is the certificate that
--              item 1 of the Part itself confers ("training of up to 350/480/720 hours conferring a final certificate of grade
--              1/2/3 from the Training Division"); whoever holds it has completed that course and has met item 1.  Rows A3, B5(1)
--              and C6 are for the holder of the LESSER, ungraded certificate.  TAKEN: the holder of the certificate of the grade sought
--              is in item 1 and nothing further is asked of them (no hours); the engine returns item 1 with the entry "the
--              certificate itself" for the certificate they hold, and A3, B5(1), C6 do not reach that certificate.  ALTERNATIVE (the
--              literal reading, the state of this module before the repair): the certificate is only a column A entry, graded over
--              general puts its holder in the ungraded row, and they are asked for up to 50, 50 or 200 hours more.  Discriminating
--              applicant: a grade 3 certificate holder seeking a grade 3 licence (item 1 against C6); likewise grade 2 for grade 2
--              (B5(1)) and grade 1 for grade 1 (A3).
--   FS11        A Division certificate of a HIGHER grade than the one sought (a grade 3 certificate seeking grade 1 or 2).  The text
--              does not say that a higher certificate stands in for the course of a lower grade.  TAKEN: it is not the certificate
--              that item 1 of the Part confers, so graded over general still puts its holder in the ungraded row (A3 for grades 2 and
--              3 seeking grade 1; B5(1) for grade 3 seeking grade 2: up to 50 hours).  ALTERNATIVE (a fortiori): a certificate of the
--              grade sought or of a higher grade meets item 1 and nothing further is asked.  An open question for a domain expert.
--   FS2 (T2)   Item 1 is headed "no prior training or experience", yet its option (2) is a certificate, which is prior
--              training; and a 5-unit certificate is named both in item 1(2) of Part B (nothing more is required) and in
--              item 5(3) of Part B (up to 50 hours).  TAKEN: item 1 is the DEFAULT item of its Part, the one that applies
--              to an applicant no other (open) item of the Part fits; a more specific item displaces it.  So B1(2) is
--              reached by nobody, because B5(3) always fits the 5-unit holder; A1(2) works, because no other item of
--              Part A fits a 3-unit holder.  ALTERNATIVES: (a) item 1 applies only to an applicant with no prior training
--              or experience at all; (b) item 1 also applies to the holder of a certificate its own column B names, so
--              B1(2) is reached and the 5-unit holder is in two items.
--   FS3 (T3)   B2 and B6 (C2 and C7) both name registration as technician (practical engineer); B2 adds the completed
--              programme with the complement course.  TAKEN: the registration-alone item reaches the registered
--              applicant who did NOT complete the programme (the pair partitions on the programme).  ALTERNATIVE: it
--              reaches every registered applicant.
--   FS4 (T5)   Part B heads column B "training or complementary studies required"; Parts A and C head it "requirements for
--              the licence sought".  The encoding reproduces column B as printed in all Parts; whether Part B's column B
--              is complementary to the prior qualification or the whole requirement changes what s 6(a)(4)(c) means, not
--              what the table says (see g2-conditions).
--   FS5 (T6)   "training of up to N hours": TAKEN a ceiling on the course; the hours the applicant must complete are not
--              stated (a named refusal).  ALTERNATIVE: exactly N.
--   FS6 (T4)   Part C item 4, column B: TAKEN the gazette (240 hours in column B).  ALTERNATIVE: the wiki's layout, in which
--              column B states nothing (a named refusal).
--   FS7        Experience (kinds B, outside IL s 10): (a) "a year of cumulative experience" is a number of days: TAKEN 365;
--              (b) the window ends the day BEFORE the application ("before the filing of the application"): ALTERNATIVE
--              it includes the application day; (c) overlapping periods are counted ONCE: ALTERNATIVE they are added.
--   FS8 (kind C, P9, T7)  The three-year note on A2, B4 and C5: from the commencement day of s 63(a)(1), an input date;
--              IL s 10(b); commencement day INCLUSIVE; IL s 10(c) not applied; tested on the application day.
--              ALTERNATIVES: IL s 10(c) applied; another anchor (the later commencement of s 63(a)(2)); the day of decision.
--   FS9        "a grade 1 licence" in column A (B3(1), C3(1), C4(1)): TAKEN a licence in force on the day of the application (the Schedule
--              does not say that a lapsed, revoked or suspended licence counts); ALTERNATIVE: any licence of the kind the register shows.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Nouns of the Schedule
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@desc An entry of column A of the Second Schedule: a prior qualification an applicant may have
DECLARE `Second Schedule column A entry` IS ONE OF
    `column A: no prior training or experience`
    `column A: a licence of the kind` HAS `the kind of licence held` IS A `Licence kind`
    `column A: a certificate` HAS `the certificate held` IS A Certificate
    `registered as a certified air-conditioning technician, and completed a programme including the complement course`
    `registered as a certified air-conditioning technician`
    `registered as an air-conditioning practical engineer, and completed a programme including the complement course`
    `registered as an air-conditioning practical engineer`
    `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch`
    `cumulative experience in work on cooling systems` HAS
        `the years of cumulative experience` IS A NUMBER
        `within the years before the application` IS A NUMBER

@desc An entry of column B of the Second Schedule: what is required for the licence sought
DECLARE `Requirement of the Second Schedule` IS ONE OF
    `training of up to` HAS
        `the ceiling on the course, in hours` IS A NUMBER
        `the certificate the training confers` IS A Certificate
    `column B: the certificate itself` HAS `the certificate that suffices` IS A Certificate
    `column B: no further requirement`

@desc One item of the Second Schedule: a row of a Part, with its columns A, B and C
DECLARE `Second Schedule item` HAS
    `the part: the licence kind it leads to` IS A `Licence kind`
    `the item number` IS A NUMBER
    `column A: any one of` IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule column A entry`
    `column B: any one of` IS A LIST OF `Requirement of the Second Schedule`
    `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN

@desc How the Second Schedule treats a Training Division certificate of the grade that the course of the Part sought itself confers, and of a higher grade (forks FS10 and FS11)
DECLARE `Reading of the Division certificate of the grade sought` IS ONE OF
    `the Division certificate of the grade sought is only an ordinary column A entry`
    `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`
    `a Division certificate of the grade sought or of a higher grade meets item 1`

@desc The readings of the Schedule that the Law's text leaves open; the field comments say which value is taken and which is the alternative
DECLARE `Reading of the Second Schedule` HAS
    `an ungraded Division certificate in column A reaches every grade` IS A BOOLEAN -- FS1: FALSE taken
    `item 1 applies only where there is no prior training or experience at all` IS A BOOLEAN -- FS2(a): FALSE taken
    `item 1 also applies to the holder of a certificate its own column B names` IS A BOOLEAN -- FS2(b): FALSE taken
    `registration alone also reaches the applicant who completed the programme` IS A BOOLEAN -- FS3: FALSE taken
    `the days that make a year of cumulative experience` IS A NUMBER -- FS7(a): 365 taken
    `work on the day of the application counts` IS A BOOLEAN -- FS7(b): FALSE taken
    `overlapping periods of work are added, not counted once` IS A BOOLEAN -- FS7(c): FALSE taken
    `a licence named in column A counts although it is no longer in force` IS A BOOLEAN -- FS9: FALSE taken
    `how a Division certificate of the grade sought is read` IS A `Reading of the Division certificate of the grade sought` -- FS10 and FS11: the middle value taken

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A NUMBER
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      g IS A BOOLEAN
      h IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS A `Reading of the Division certificate of the grade sought`
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`a reading of the Second Schedule with` a b c d e f g h i MEANS
    `Reading of the Second Schedule` WITH
        `an ungraded Division certificate in column A reaches every grade` IS a
        `item 1 applies only where there is no prior training or experience at all` IS b
        `item 1 also applies to the holder of a certificate its own column B names` IS c
        `registration alone also reaches the applicant who completed the programme` IS d
        `the days that make a year of cumulative experience` IS e
        `work on the day of the application counts` IS f
        `overlapping periods of work are added, not counted once` IS g
        `a licence named in column A counts although it is no longer in force` IS h
        `how a Division certificate of the grade sought is read` IS i

-- The reading taken, and one named alternative for each fork.
@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading of the Second Schedule taken` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 365 FALSE FALSE FALSE `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with the ungraded certificate rows reaching every grade (FS1)` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 365 FALSE FALSE FALSE `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with item 1 only for applicants with no prior training or experience at all (FS2a)` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 365 FALSE FALSE FALSE `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with item 1 also open to the holder of a certificate its column B names (FS2b)` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 365 FALSE FALSE FALSE `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with registration alone reaching every registered applicant (FS3)` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 365 FALSE FALSE FALSE `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVEN `the days in a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with a year of cumulative experience counted in days (FS7a)` `the days in a year` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the days in a year` FALSE FALSE FALSE `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with work on the day of the application counted (FS7b)` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 365 TRUE FALSE FALSE `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with a licence named in column A counting although it has lapsed (FS9)` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 365 FALSE FALSE TRUE `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with overlapping periods of work added (FS7c)` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 365 FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 365 FALSE FALSE FALSE `the Division certificate of the grade sought is only an ordinary column A entry`

@ref Second Schedule, the readings registered as forks FS1 to FS11 (FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2)
GIVETH A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
`the reading with a Division certificate of a higher grade also meeting item 1 (FS11)` MEANS `a reading of the Second Schedule with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 365 FALSE FALSE FALSE `a Division certificate of the grade sought or of a higher grade meets item 1`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The Second Schedule as data: Part A, grade 1 licence
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§ `The Second Schedule — Part A: grade 1 licence`

-- S2.A (heading, inert).  The heading names the licence kind that the items below lead to; that fact is the field
-- `the part: the licence kind it leads to` of every item of the Part.

-- S2.A.1: item 1, no prior training or experience: one of (1) training of up to 350 hours conferring a grade 1
-- certificate, or (2) a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units.
-- src:566 | {{ח:קטע3|תוספת 2 חלק א|חלק א׳: רישיון דרגה 1}}
-- src:571 | <tr id="תוספת 2 חלק א פרט 1"><td>
-- src:572 | {{ח:תת|1.}} בלא הכשרה או ניסיון קודמים
-- src:573 | </td><td>
-- src:574 | {{ח:ת}} אחת מאלה:
-- src:575 | {{ח:תת|(1)}} הכשרה של עד 350 שעות המקנה תעודת גמר קירור ומיזוג אוויר דרגה 1 מהאגף להכשרה מקצועית;
-- src:576 | {{ח:תת|(2)}} תעודת גמר המעידה על לימודי בקרת אקלים ברמה של 3 יחידות לימוד (מקצוע התמחות) ממשרד החינוך
-- src:577 | </td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
@ref S2.A.1 (src:571-577)
GIVETH A `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule, Part A, item 1` MEANS
    `Second Schedule item` WITH
        `the part: the licence kind it leads to` IS `grade 1 licence`
        `the item number` IS 1
        `column A: any one of` IS LIST `column A: no prior training or experience`
        `column B: any one of` IS LIST
            (`training of up to` 350 `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)
            , (`column B: the certificate itself` `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`)
        `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day` IS FALSE

-- S2.A.2 and its column C note S2.A.2/colC: item 2, prior experience: any one of (1) a year of cumulative experience out of
-- three years before the application, (2) three years of cumulative experience out of seven years before it: training of
-- up to 220 hours conferring a grade 1 certificate.  Column C: this provision is valid for three years from the commencement
-- of the Law as stated in s 63(a)(1).
-- src:578 | <tr id="תוספת 2 חלק א פרט 2"><td>
-- src:579 | {{ח:תת|2.}} כל אחד מאלה:
-- src:580 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} שנת ניסיון במצטבר מתוך שלוש שנים בעבודות במערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר טרם הגשת הבקשה לרישיון;
-- src:581 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} שלוש שנות ניסיון במצטבר מתוך שבע שנים בעבודות במערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר טרם הגשת הבקשה לרישיון
-- src:582 | </td><td>
-- src:583 | {{ח:ת}} הכשרה של עד 220 שעות המקנה תעודת גמר קירור ומיזוג אוויר דרגה 1 מהאגף להכשרה מקצועית
-- src:584 | </td><td>
-- src:585 | {{ח:ת}} הוראה זו תעמוד בתוקף לתקופה של שלוש שנים מיום תחילתו של חוק זה, כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 63|בסעיף 63(א)(1)}}
-- src:586 | </td></tr>
@ref S2.A.2 and S2.A.2/colC (src:578-586)
GIVETH A `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule, Part A, item 2` MEANS
    `Second Schedule item` WITH
        `the part: the licence kind it leads to` IS `grade 1 licence`
        `the item number` IS 2
        `column A: any one of` IS LIST
            (`cumulative experience in work on cooling systems` 1 3)
            , (`cumulative experience in work on cooling systems` 3 7)
        `column B: any one of` IS LIST (`training of up to` 220 `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)
        `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day` IS TRUE

-- S2.A.3: item 3, a certificate in refrigeration and air-conditioning studies from the Training Division (no grade stated):
