-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Column C: the three-year note on the experience items (kind C, trap T7)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§ `The Second Schedule — column C, the three-year note on the experience items`

-- "This provision shall stand in force for a period of three years from the day this Law comes into force, as stated in
-- s 63(a)(1)."  (A2: line 585; B4: line 624; C5: line 678.)  KIND C: a period counted from another date, here the
-- commencement day, itself an input from group G7 (integration point IP2); the Second Schedule never hard-codes it.
-- IL s 10(b): three years after an event on the commencement day end on the same-numbered day three years later, and
-- that day is inside the period.  FS8: the commencement day itself is the first day the item is in force (an item of a
-- Law is in force from the day the Law commences, s 21 of the Interpretation Law fixing only the hour), so the day the
-- module calls "the first day of a period counted from an event" (the day after) is NOT used here.  IL s 10(c) is not
-- applied to a period of validity of a provision (the fleet's ruling 4); the alternative applies it.
-- src:585 | {{ח:ת}} הוראה זו תעמוד בתוקף לתקופה של שלוש שנים מיום תחילתו של חוק זה, כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 63|בסעיף 63(א)(1)}}
@ref S2.A.2/colC, S2.B.4/colC, S2.C.5/colC (src:585)
@desc The last day on which the three-year note of the Second Schedule keeps its experience items in force: three years after the commencement day (Interpretation Law s 10(b))
GIVEN `the commencement day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Second Schedule column C — the last day of the three years beginning on` `the commencement day` MEANS
    `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` `the commencement day`

@ref S2.A.2/colC, S2.B.4/colC, S2.C.5/colC (src:585)
GIVEN `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `the calendar of rest days` IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`Second Schedule column C (Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied) — the last day of the three years beginning on` `the commencement day` `, with` `the calendar of rest days` MEANS
    `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` `the commencement day`
        `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are`
        (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (`the calendar of rest days`'s `days of rest, recess or holiday`))

@ref S2.A.2/colC, S2.B.4/colC, S2.C.5/colC (src:585)
GIVEN `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule column C — the experience items are in force on the day` `the commencement day` day MEANS
    day AT MOST `Second Schedule column C — the last day of the three years beginning on` `the commencement day`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Column A: does the applicant meet an entry?
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§ `The Second Schedule — column A, who falls in an item`

@desc Everything the engine needs to ask what the Second Schedule requires of an applicant: the reading, the application, the schedule in use, the commencement day and the day the three-year note is tested on
DECLARE `Second Schedule case` HAS
    `the reading` IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
    `the application` IS AN Application
    `the schedule in use` IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
    `the commencement day` IS A DATE
    `the day the three-year note is tested on` IS A DATE

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
      application IS AN Application
      schedule IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
      commencement IS A DATE
      tested IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Second Schedule case`
`a Second Schedule case` reading application schedule commencement tested MEANS
    `Second Schedule case` WITH
        `the reading` IS reading
        `the application` IS application
        `the schedule in use` IS schedule
        `the commencement day` IS commencement
        `the day the three-year note is tested on` IS tested

-- Certificates.  The Training Division's certificates are the four of grade 1, 2, 3 and "no grade stated"; the
-- vocational school for youth and the Ministry of Education certificates are others.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN certificate IS A Certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — is a graded Training Division certificate` certificate MEANS
    CONSIDER certificate
    WHEN `a Training Division certificate of grade 1` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Training Division certificate of grade 2` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Training Division certificate of grade 3` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN certificate IS A Certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — is a Training Division certificate, graded or not` certificate MEANS
        `Second Schedule — is a graded Training Division certificate` certificate
    OR  certificate EQUALS `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`

-- The certificates that a GRADED entry of column A names, in a list of items.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN entry IS A `Second Schedule column A entry`
GIVETH A LIST OF Certificate
`Second Schedule — the graded certificate named by the entry` entry MEANS
    CONSIDER entry
    WHEN `column A: a certificate` named THEN
        IF   `Second Schedule — is a graded Training Division certificate` named
        THEN LIST named
        ELSE EMPTY
    OTHERWISE EMPTY

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN items IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A LIST OF Certificate
`Second Schedule — the graded certificates named in column A of` items MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN item YIELD concat (map `Second Schedule — the graded certificate named by the entry` (item's `column A: any one of`))) items)

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN kind IS A `Licence kind`
      `the schedule in use` IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule — the items of the part leading to` kind `in` `the schedule in use` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the part: the licence kind it leads to` EQUALS kind) `the schedule in use`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A `Licence kind`
`Second Schedule — the part sought in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the kind of licence sought`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule — the items of the part sought in` `the case` MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the items of the part leading to` (`Second Schedule — the part sought in` `the case`) `in` (`the case`'s `the schedule in use`)

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH AN Applicant
`Second Schedule — the applicant in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the applicant`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A DATE
`Second Schedule — the day of the application in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the day of the application`

-- Accessors.  (A genitive cannot follow a parenthesised call, so each field read goes through a rule of its own.)
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A LIST OF Certificate
`Second Schedule — the certificates held in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the applicant`'s `certificates held`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A LIST OF Licence
`Second Schedule — the licences held in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the applicant`'s `licences held`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`Second Schedule — the periods of work in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the applicant`'s `periods of work on cooling systems`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the registration as a technician is recorded in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the applicant`'s `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the registration as a practical engineer is recorded in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the applicant`'s `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the registration as a mechanical engineer is recorded in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the applicant`'s `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the programme with the complement course is recorded in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the application`'s `the applicant`'s `completed a study programme that includes the complement course`

-- Whether the applicant holds the very certificate named.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
      certificate IS A Certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant holds the certificate` certificate MEANS
    elem certificate (`Second Schedule — the certificates held in` `the case`)

-- Whether the applicant holds a licence of the kind that is in force on the day of the application.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant holds a licence of the kind` kind `in force on the day of the application` MEANS
    any (GIVEN licence YIELD
                licence's `the kind of licence` EQUALS kind
            AND (    `the case`'s `the reading`'s `a licence named in column A counts although it is no longer in force`
                 OR  `the licence is in force on` licence (`Second Schedule — the day of the application in` `the case`)))
        (`Second Schedule — the licences held in` `the case`)

-- FS7: the experience tests.  KIND B: a period counted BACKWARDS from the application, which Interpretation Law s 10
-- does not cover (s 10 speaks of periods from a day or after an event), so the time module is not used and plain date
-- comparison is.  The window starts on the same calendar date N years before the day of the application, rebuilt from
-- its components (a 29 February start rolls to 1 March, the first day on which the same-numbered day after the start
-- falls on or after the application day) and ends the day before the application ("before the filing of the application").
@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN years IS A NUMBER
      `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A DATE
`Second Schedule — the first day of the window of` years `years before the application in` `the case` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY (`Second Schedule — the day of the application in` `the case`))
         (DATE_MONTH (`Second Schedule — the day of the application in` `the case`))
         (DATE_YEAR (`Second Schedule — the day of the application in` `the case`) MINUS years)

@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Second Schedule — the number of the last day of the window in` `the case` MEANS
    IF   `the case`'s `the reading`'s `work on the day of the application counts`
    THEN Day (`Second Schedule — the day of the application in` `the case`)
    ELSE Day (`Second Schedule — the day of the application in` `the case`) MINUS 1

@desc A stretch of days given as day numbers, first and last inclusive
DECLARE `Second Schedule day span` HAS
    `the first day number` IS A NUMBER
    `the last day number` IS A NUMBER

-- The stretch of one period of work that lies inside a window, as day numbers; a period wholly outside gives a span
-- with its last day before its first (length zero).
@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN `the first day number of the window` IS A NUMBER
      `the last day number of the window` IS A NUMBER
      period IS A `Period of work on cooling systems`
GIVETH A `Second Schedule day span`
`Second Schedule — the part of the window between` `the first day number of the window` `and` `the last day number of the window` `covered by` period MEANS
    `Second Schedule day span` WITH
        `the first day number` IS
            IF   Day (period's `first day of the period`) AT LEAST `the first day number of the window`
            THEN Day (period's `first day of the period`)
            ELSE `the first day number of the window`
        `the last day number` IS
            IF   Day (period's `last day of the period`) AT MOST `the last day number of the window`
            THEN Day (period's `last day of the period`)
            ELSE `the last day number of the window`

@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN span IS A `Second Schedule day span`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the span is not empty` span MEANS
    span's `the first day number` AT MOST span's `the last day number`

@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN span IS A `Second Schedule day span`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Second Schedule — the number of days in the span` span MEANS
    (span's `the last day number` MINUS span's `the first day number`) PLUS 1

-- Insertion sort of spans by their first day.
@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN span IS A `Second Schedule day span`
      spans IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule day span`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule day span`
`Second Schedule — the sorted spans with` span `inserted into` spans MEANS
    CONSIDER spans
    WHEN EMPTY THEN LIST span
    WHEN s FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   span's `the first day number` AT MOST s's `the first day number`
        THEN span FOLLOWED BY (s FOLLOWED BY rest)
        ELSE s FOLLOWED BY (`Second Schedule — the sorted spans with` span `inserted into` rest)

@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN spans IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule day span`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule day span`
`Second Schedule — the spans sorted by first day` spans MEANS
    foldr (GIVEN span, sorted YIELD `Second Schedule — the sorted spans with` span `inserted into` sorted) EMPTY spans

-- Days of a sorted list of spans not already covered up to day `covered`, each day once.
@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN covered IS A NUMBER
      spans IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule day span`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Second Schedule — the days in the sorted spans after day` covered `, each counted once, in` spans MEANS
    CONSIDER spans
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN s FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF   s's `the last day number` GREATER THAN covered
         THEN (s's `the last day number`
               MINUS (IF s's `the first day number` GREATER THAN covered THEN s's `the first day number` ELSE covered PLUS 1))
              PLUS 1
         ELSE 0)
        PLUS `Second Schedule — the days in the sorted spans after day`
                (IF s's `the last day number` GREATER THAN covered THEN s's `the last day number` ELSE covered)
                `, each counted once, in` rest

@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
@desc The days of work on cooling systems, among the periods the applicant lists, that fall within the given number of years before the application; the periods are clipped to the window, and each day counts once unless the reading adds overlapping periods
GIVEN years IS A NUMBER
      `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Second Schedule — the cumulative days of work in the` years `years before the application in` `the case` MEANS
    IF   `the case`'s `the reading`'s `overlapping periods of work are added, not counted once`
    THEN sum (map `Second Schedule — the number of days in the span` clipped)
    ELSE `Second Schedule — the days in the sorted spans after day` 0 `, each counted once, in` (`Second Schedule — the spans sorted by first day` clipped)
    WHERE
        `window start` MEANS Day (`Second Schedule — the first day of the window of` years `years before the application in` `the case`)
        `window end` MEANS `Second Schedule — the number of the last day of the window in` `the case`
        clipped MEANS
            filter `Second Schedule — the span is not empty`
                (map (GIVEN period YIELD `Second Schedule — the part of the window between` `window start` `and` `window end` `covered by` period)
                     (`Second Schedule — the periods of work in` `the case`))

@ref Second Schedule, column A: cumulative experience within the years before the application (kind B, outside IL s 10)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
      `the years of cumulative experience` IS A NUMBER
      `the years before the application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant has` `the years of cumulative experience` `years of cumulative experience within the` `the years before the application` `years before the application` MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the cumulative days of work in the` `the years before the application` `years before the application in` `the case`
        AT LEAST `the years of cumulative experience` TIMES `the case`'s `the reading`'s `the days that make a year of cumulative experience`

-- FS10 and FS11.  The Division certificate that item 1 of each Part itself confers is grade 1 in Part A (350 hours), grade 2 in Part B
-- (480 hours) and grade 3 in Part C (720 hours); the certificates of a higher grade than the Part sought are the other graded ones.
@ref Second Schedule, Parts A to C, item 1, column B (fork FS10)
GIVEN kind IS A `Licence kind`
GIVETH A Certificate
`Second Schedule — the Division certificate that item 1 of the Part leading to` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `grade 1 licence` THEN `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`
    WHEN `grade 2 licence` THEN `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`
    WHEN `grade 3 licence` THEN `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`

@ref Second Schedule, Parts A to C, item 1, column B (fork FS11)
GIVEN kind IS A `Licence kind`
GIVETH A LIST OF Certificate
`Second Schedule — the Division certificates of a higher grade than the Part leading to` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `grade 1 licence` THEN LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`, `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`
    WHEN `grade 2 licence` THEN LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`
    WHEN `grade 3 licence` THEN EMPTY

-- The Division certificates that meet item 1 of the Part sought under a reading: none on the literal reading, the certificate of the
-- grade sought on the reading taken, and that certificate with the higher grades on the a fortiori reading.
@ref Second Schedule, Parts A to C, item 1 (forks FS10 and FS11)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A LIST OF Certificate
`Second Schedule — the Division certificates that meet item 1 in` `the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case`'s `the reading`'s `how a Division certificate of the grade sought is read`
    WHEN `the Division certificate of the grade sought is only an ordinary column A entry` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `the Division certificate of the grade sought meets item 1` THEN
        LIST `Second Schedule — the Division certificate that item 1 of the Part leading to` (`Second Schedule — the part sought in` `the case`)
    WHEN `a Division certificate of the grade sought or of a higher grade meets item 1` THEN
        append (LIST `Second Schedule — the Division certificate that item 1 of the Part leading to` (`Second Schedule — the part sought in` `the case`))
               (`Second Schedule — the Division certificates of a higher grade than the Part leading to` (`Second Schedule — the part sought in` `the case`))

-- The certificates of that list that the applicant holds.
@ref Second Schedule, Parts A to C, item 1 (forks FS10 and FS11)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A LIST OF Certificate
`Second Schedule — the certificates held that meet item 1 in` `the case` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN held YIELD `Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant holds the certificate` held)
           (`Second Schedule — the Division certificates that meet item 1 in` `the case`)

-- The entries of column A.  An entry "no prior training or experience" is the business of the item, not of the entry
-- (below), so it is FALSE here.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
      entry IS A `Second Schedule column A entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the applicant in` `the case` `meets the entry` entry MEANS
    CONSIDER entry
    WHEN `column A: no prior training or experience` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `column A: a licence of the kind` kind THEN
        `Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant holds a licence of the kind` kind `in force on the day of the application`
    WHEN `column A: a certificate` certificate THEN
        IF   certificate EQUALS `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`
        THEN
            -- FS10 and FS11: the certificate that item 1 of the Part itself confers (and, on the a fortiori reading, a higher one) is not
            -- an entry of the ungraded rows on the readings that let it meet item 1; this holds on both branches of FS1.
            IF   `the case`'s `the reading`'s `an ungraded Division certificate in column A reaches every grade`
            THEN any (GIVEN held YIELD
                            `Second Schedule — is a Training Division certificate, graded or not` held
                        AND NOT elem held (`Second Schedule — the Division certificates that meet item 1 in` `the case`))
                     (`Second Schedule — the certificates held in` `the case`)
            ELSE any (GIVEN held YIELD
                            `Second Schedule — is a Training Division certificate, graded or not` held
                        AND NOT elem held (`Second Schedule — the graded certificates named in column A of` (`Second Schedule — the items of the part sought in` `the case`))
                        AND NOT elem held (`Second Schedule — the Division certificates that meet item 1 in` `the case`))
                     (`Second Schedule — the certificates held in` `the case`)
        ELSE `Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant holds the certificate` certificate
    WHEN `registered as a certified air-conditioning technician, and completed a programme including the complement course` THEN
            `Second Schedule — the registration as a technician is recorded in` `the case`
        AND `Second Schedule — the programme with the complement course is recorded in` `the case`
    WHEN `registered as a certified air-conditioning technician` THEN
            `Second Schedule — the registration as a technician is recorded in` `the case`
        AND (    `the case`'s `the reading`'s `registration alone also reaches the applicant who completed the programme`
             OR  NOT `Second Schedule — the programme with the complement course is recorded in` `the case`)
    WHEN `registered as an air-conditioning practical engineer, and completed a programme including the complement course` THEN
            `Second Schedule — the registration as a practical engineer is recorded in` `the case`
        AND `Second Schedule — the programme with the complement course is recorded in` `the case`
    WHEN `registered as an air-conditioning practical engineer` THEN
            `Second Schedule — the registration as a practical engineer is recorded in` `the case`
        AND (    `the case`'s `the reading`'s `registration alone also reaches the applicant who completed the programme`
             OR  NOT `Second Schedule — the programme with the complement course is recorded in` `the case`)
    WHEN `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch` THEN
        `Second Schedule — the registration as a mechanical engineer is recorded in` `the case`
    WHEN `cumulative experience in work on cooling systems` years within THEN
        `Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant has` years `years of cumulative experience within the` within `years before the application`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The items: which of them apply?
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§ `The Second Schedule — which items apply to an application`

-- The three-year note: an item carrying it is open until the last day of the three years from the commencement day.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
      item IS A `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the item is open` item MEANS
    IF   item's `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day`
    THEN `Second Schedule column C — the experience items are in force on the day`
             (`the case`'s `the commencement day`) (`the case`'s `the day the three-year note is tested on`)
    ELSE TRUE

-- An item whose column A is "no prior training or experience" is the item 1 of its Part (FS2).
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN item IS A `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — is an item headed no prior training or experience` item MEANS
    any (GIVEN entry YIELD entry EQUALS `column A: no prior training or experience`) (item's `column A: any one of`)

-- Item other than item 1: it applies if it is open and the applicant meets any one of its column A entries.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN item IS A `Second Schedule item`
      `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — a specific item` item `applies in` `the case` MEANS
        `Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the item is open` item
    AND any (GIVEN entry YIELD `Second Schedule — the applicant in` `the case` `meets the entry` entry) (item's `column A: any one of`)

-- No prior training or experience at all: nothing in the record that column A could count.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN applicant IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — has no prior training or experience at all` applicant MEANS
        null (applicant's `certificates held`)
    AND null (applicant's `licences held`)
    AND null (applicant's `periods of work on cooling systems`)
    AND NOT applicant's `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning`
    AND NOT applicant's `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning`
    AND NOT applicant's `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch`
    AND NOT applicant's `completed a study programme that includes the complement course`

-- Whether the applicant holds a certificate that the item's own column B names as sufficient ("the certificate itself").
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
      item IS A `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant holds a certificate that column B of` item `names as sufficient` MEANS
    any (GIVEN requirement YIELD
            CONSIDER requirement
            WHEN `column B: the certificate itself` certificate THEN `Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant holds the certificate` certificate
            OTHERWISE FALSE)
        (item's `column B: any one of`)

-- An item that is not an item 1 and applies (used to decide whether the default item 1 is displaced).
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN item IS A `Second Schedule item`
      `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — an item other than item 1` item `applies in` `the case` MEANS
        NOT `Second Schedule — is an item headed no prior training or experience` item
    AND `Second Schedule — a specific item` item `applies in` `the case`

-- Item 1 (FS2).  TAKEN: the default item of its Part, applying to an applicant that no other item of the Part fits.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN item IS A `Second Schedule item`
      `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the item 1` item `applies in` `the case` MEANS
        (    IF   `the case`'s `the reading`'s `item 1 applies only where there is no prior training or experience at all`
             THEN `Second Schedule — has no prior training or experience at all` (`Second Schedule — the applicant in` `the case`)
             ELSE NOT any (GIVEN other YIELD `Second Schedule — an item other than item 1` other `applies in` `the case`)
                          (`Second Schedule — the items of the part sought in` `the case`))
    OR  (    `the case`'s `the reading`'s `item 1 also applies to the holder of a certificate its own column B names`
         AND `Second Schedule — in` `the case` `the applicant holds a certificate that column B of` item `names as sufficient`)
    -- FS10 and FS11: whoever holds the certificate that the course of item 1 confers has completed that course and has met item 1,
    -- whatever other item also fits them.
    OR  NOT null (`Second Schedule — the certificates held that meet item 1 in` `the case`)

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN item IS A `Second Schedule item`
      `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the item` item `applies in` `the case` MEANS
    IF   `Second Schedule — is an item headed no prior training or experience` item
    THEN `Second Schedule — the item 1` item `applies in` `the case`
    ELSE `Second Schedule — a specific item` item `applies in` `the case`

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
@desc The items of the Second Schedule, in the Schedule's order, that apply to the application under the case's reading; every item that applies is returned, and where two do their column B entries are both there
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule — the items that apply in` `the case` MEANS
    map (GIVEN item YIELD `Second Schedule — the item as read:` item `for the applicant in` `the case`)
        (filter (GIVEN item YIELD `Second Schedule — the item` item `applies in` `the case`)
                (`Second Schedule — the items of the part sought in` `the case`))

-- FS10 and FS11.  Item 1 as it reads for an applicant who holds the certificate that its course confers: column B gains the entry "the
-- certificate itself" for each such certificate held.  Every other item, and item 1 for everyone else, is returned as the Schedule prints it.
-- The added entry is the whole content of the reading: the Schedule prints no such entry, the reading supplies it.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, Parts A to C, item 1, column B (forks FS10 and FS11)
GIVEN item IS A `Second Schedule item`
      `the case` IS A `Second Schedule case`
GIVETH A `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule — the item as read:` item `for the applicant in` `the case` MEANS
    IF   `Second Schedule — is an item headed no prior training or experience` item
         AND NOT null (`Second Schedule — the certificates held that meet item 1 in` `the case`)
    THEN `Second Schedule item` WITH
             `the part: the licence kind it leads to` IS item's `the part: the licence kind it leads to`
             `the item number` IS item's `the item number`
             `column A: any one of` IS item's `column A: any one of`
             `column B: any one of` IS append (item's `column B: any one of`)
                                              (map (GIVEN held YIELD `column B: the certificate itself` held)
                                                   (`Second Schedule — the certificates held that meet item 1 in` `the case`))
             `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day` IS item's `column C: valid for three years from the commencement day`
    ELSE item

-- Named refusal, returned never stored.
@ref Second Schedule: a named refusal where the sources do not answer
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Second Schedule gives no item for this applicant` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Second Schedule gives no item for this applicant (no item of the Part sought applies to the application on the reading taken)"

@ref Second Schedule: a named refusal where the sources do not answer
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`column B of the item states no requirement` MEANS
    REFUSE "column B of the item states no requirement (on the wiki's layout of Part C item 4 the 240 hours stand in column A)"

-- The headline answer (integration point IP6): the items of the Part sought that apply, each with its requirements.
-- On the reading taken item 1 is the default of every Part, so the list is never empty and the named refusal below is
-- unreachable; it is reachable under a reading where item 1 is not the default (FS2a), through the function that takes the reading.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
      application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule — the training required for the licence sought under` `the reading` `by` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day` MEANS
    IF   null (`Second Schedule — the items that apply under` `the reading` `to` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day`)
    THEN `the Second Schedule gives no item for this applicant`
    ELSE `Second Schedule — the items that apply under` `the reading` `to` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day`

-- src:88 | {{ח:תתת|(4)}} מתקיים בו אחד התנאים שלהלן, והכול בהתאם לתנאים {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 2|שבתוספת השנייה}}:
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule (src:88)
@export The items of the Second Schedule that apply to a licence application (prior training and experience in column A, the training or certificate required in column B, hours being the ceiling of the course), on the reading taken; the application's own day is the day the three-year note on the experience items is tested on
GIVEN application IS AN Application @desc The licence application: the applicant and what they hold, the kind of licence sought and the day of the application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE @desc The commencement day of the Law under s 63(a)(1), from which the three-year note of the experience items runs
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`training required for the licence sought` application `the commencement day` MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the training required for the licence sought under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `by` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day`

-- The alternatives, each the same engine with another reading, schedule or day.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
      application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule — the items that apply under` `the reading` `to` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day` MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the items that apply in`
        (`a Second Schedule case` `the reading` application `the Second Schedule` `the commencement day` (application's `the day of the application`))

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule (Part C item 4 as the wiki prints it) — the items that apply to` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day` MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the items that apply in`
        (`a Second Schedule case` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` application
             `the Second Schedule with Part C item 4 as the wiki prints it` `the commencement day` (application's `the day of the application`))

@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, columns A, B and C (the engine that reads the Schedule)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `the day of decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`Second Schedule (the three-year note tested on the day of decision) — the items that apply to` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day` `, decided on` `the day of decision` MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the items that apply in`
        (`a Second Schedule case` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` application `the Second Schedule` `the commencement day` `the day of decision`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Column B: what each entry asks (trap T6)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§ `The Second Schedule — column B, the hours`

@ref Second Schedule, column B: "training of up to N hours" (trap T6)
GIVEN items IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Requirement of the Second Schedule`
`Second Schedule — the requirements in column B of` items MEANS
    IF   null (concat (map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `column B: any one of`) items))
    THEN `column B of the item states no requirement`
    ELSE concat (map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `column B: any one of`) items)

-- FS5.  "Training of up to N hours" is a ceiling on the course the Training Division runs: the text does not say how many
-- hours an applicant must complete, so that is a named refusal; the ceiling is what the text gives.
@ref Second Schedule, column B: "training of up to N hours" (trap T6)
GIVEN requirement IS A `Requirement of the Second Schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Second Schedule — the ceiling on the hours of` requirement MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
    WHEN `training of up to` ceiling certificate THEN ceiling
    OTHERWISE `this requirement of column B is not a course of training`

@ref Second Schedule: a named refusal where the sources do not answer
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this requirement of column B is not a course of training` MEANS
    REFUSE "this requirement of column B is not a course of training, so it has no ceiling on hours"

@ref Second Schedule: a named refusal where the sources do not answer
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Second Schedule states only a ceiling on the hours, not a number of hours the applicant must complete` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Second Schedule states only a ceiling on the hours of the course (training of up to N hours), not a number of hours the applicant must complete"

@ref Second Schedule, column B: "training of up to N hours" (trap T6)
GIVEN requirement IS A `Requirement of the Second Schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Second Schedule — the hours the applicant must complete under` requirement MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
    WHEN `training of up to` ceiling certificate THEN `the Second Schedule states only a ceiling on the hours, not a number of hours the applicant must complete`
    OTHERWISE 0

-- FS5, the alternative: "up to N hours" read as exactly N.
@ref Second Schedule, column B: "training of up to N hours" (trap T6)
GIVEN requirement IS A `Requirement of the Second Schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Second Schedule (up to N read as exactly N) — the hours the applicant must complete under` requirement MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
    WHEN `training of up to` ceiling certificate THEN ceiling
    OTHERWISE 0
